s a merge commit sha on stdin and prints that merge's attestation statement as JSON on exit 0; nothing on a non-zero exit. The doctor's fifth proof runs it once per merged, fully-staged item to require a statement in the store.\\\",\\nschema/manifest.schema.json:99:          \\\"description\\\": \\\"A commit sha. A merge at or before it predates the tenant's merge queue and is named by the doctor's fifth proof as before the window rather than failed.\\\",\\nattest/specs/158/spec.md:7:Amended 2026-09-18 after #169 landed on `main` under this item's approved tree: an item's merge is the merge on the default branch's first-parent line (read from `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD`, refused by name when the ref is unset), so the proof names an item with no such merge in `not_merged` rather than skipping or failing it, fails by name on the walk's refusal, and the fixtures set the ref they depend on. The approval bound to the previous spec commit expires with this amendment, as the product requires.\\nattest/specs/158/spec.md:9:Amended again 2026-09-18 after build-05: the doctor job's pytest step ran `gh` with no token, the attestation command exited 2, and proof six called #151's sealed merge unsealed. Exit 2 from the command is \\\"the store could not be read\\\", a fact the proof now reports as `not read` by item, with the command and its exit in the reason, never as `unsealed`; and the doctor job carries `GH_TOKEN` at the job level so every step that runs the doctor can read the store. The approval expires again with this amendment.\\n.attavo/bin/forge-attestation:20:test -n \\\"$sha\\\" || exit 2\\n.attavo/bin/forge-attestation:22:repo=$(gh repo view --json nameWithOwner --jq .nameWithOwner 2>/dev/null) || exit 2\\nbin/attavo:53:                             the store itself could not be read, reported\\nbin/attavo:1454:    anything but a JSON object -- exit 2 means the store itself could not\\nbin/attavo:1517:                           f\\\"the store could not be read; {cmd!r