supply a record\\n# found missing there. attest's stdout -- the statement, or a not-yet or\\n# zero-item line -- is captured to a plain file, and the attest step\\n# itself reads whether that file parses as a JSON object into its own\\n# `statement` output: a python3 -c json.load check, its exit status read\\n# into the output, never a grep -- a grep would say yes for any line that\\n# merely looks like JSON, which a not-yet line's stage names could. The\\n# not-yet and zero-item lines are prose, not JSON, and a merge group can\\n# carry no item exactly as easily as a pull request can; without this\\n# check the steps below would hand actions/attest that prose the moment\\n# the pin lane's own installing merge -- which touches no item -- reached\\n# the queue.\\n#\\n# Only on merge_group -- github.sha there resolves to the commit that\\n# will actually land on main, not the merge queue's own temporary ref --\\n# and only when attest's own output says the captured file is a\\n# statement, two further steps run: a sha256 digest of that commit's own\\n# sha text (deterministic and reproducible from the sha alone), and\\n# actions/attest@v2, signing attest's printed statement as the predicate,\\n# env.ATTAVO_ATTESTATION_PREDICATE_TYPE, over that digest. That variable\\n# is action.yml's own export of the schema's $id, never typed here (issue\\n# #117: v0.18.0 moved the $id from .../v1 to .../v2, and this template's\\n# own copy of the literal did not move with it). Signing here replaces\\n# the post-merge attest workflow this product shipped before (issue #69):\\n# the four stage records are the evidence, and the bundle actions/attest@v2\\n# writes to the forge's attestation store is the seal over them -- no\\n# attestation record is ever written to the tree.\\n#\\n# Neither step carries continue-on-error. Ruled: a merge without a\\n# signature is unattested, and the product's claim is that nothing merges\\n# unattested, so a signing failure fails this required context and the\\n# merge does not happen. This reverses the 2026-09-09 refusal-tolerance\\n# ruling for the step that used to patch a record's signed field either\\n# way; there is no record left for that patch to write to, and a tenant\\n# whose signing provider is unavailable un-requires this context as its\\n# own act, on its own ledger -- not a default this template supplies.\\n#\\n# This step is not folded into attavo-spec-gate.yml's job, for two\\n# reasons: that job skips an ordinary pull request from any branch that\\n# doesn't start with attavo/ (issue #12), and every step after its skip\\n# step is skipped on a record-only commit. An approval push is a\\n# record-only commit -- including a re-approval after a build, the exact\\n# shape that broke the chain on tenant zero (approval-07, issue #62) --\\n# so folding coherence into that job would skip the check on precisely\\n# the commit most likely to need it. Coherence has neither restriction:\\n# it runs on any pull request, record-only commit or not, and reports its\\n# own required context so a tenant can gate the merge queue on it without\\n# widening the spec-gate job's guards.\\n#\\n# actions/checkout@v4 takes no ref: -- the pull_request and merge_group\\n# events default to the merge commit checkout already needs, the same\\n# tree `attavo attest` reads git diff --name-only HEAD^1 HEAD against.\\n# fetch-depth: 0 keeps that first parent reachable.\\n#\\n# No app token is minted and nothing is pushed: attest prints, it never\\n# writes, and the signed statement lives in the forge's attestation\\n# store, not in a commit this job makes.\\nname: Attavo coherence\\n\\non:\\n  pull_request:\\n    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\\n  merge_group:\\n\\njobs:\\n  coherence:\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    permissions:\\n      contents: read\\n      id-token: write\\n      attestations: write\\n    steps:\\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\\n        with:\\n          fetch-depth: 0\\n\\n      - uses: attavo/attavo@v0.25.0\\n\\n      - name: attavo attest\\n        id: attest\\n        run: |\\n          attavo attest ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && '--partial' || '' }} > \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/attestation.json\\\"\\n          if python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; sys.exit(0 if isinstance(json.load(open(sys.argv[1])), dict) else 1)\\\" \\\"$RUNNER_TEMP/attestation.json\\\" 2>/dev/null; then\\n            echo \\\"statement=true\\\" >> \\\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\\\"\\n          else\\n            echo \\\"statement=false\\\" >> \\\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\\\"\\n          fi\\n\\n      - name: Compute the merge commit's subject digest\\n        id: subject\\n        if: github.event_name == 'merge_group' && steps.attest.outputs.statement == 'true'\\n        run: echo \\\"digest=sha256:$(printf '%s' \\\"${{ github.sha }}\\\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\\\" >> \\\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\\\"\\n\\n      - name: Sign the attestation record\\n        id: sign\\n        if: github.event_name == 'merge_group' && steps.attest.outputs.statement == 'true'\\n        uses: actions/attest@v2\\n        with:\\n          subject-name: ${{ github.sha }}\\n          subject-digest: ${{ steps.subject.outputs.digest }}\\n          predicate-type: ${{ env.ATTAVO_ATTESTATION_PREDICATE_TYPE }}\\n          predicate-path: ${{ runner.temp }}/attestation.json\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-k5qy4Rjw' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-QbfBhcwr' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n## Problem\\n\\n`attavo doctor` reported done on this repository on 2026-09-17 while none of its three traversals (#106, #148, #153) had a statement in the attestation store: `main` had classic protection and no merge queue, every merge was direct, the coherence workflow's `merge_group` trigger never fired, and proof two holds on the four stage records with the chain held without asking whether the merge was sealed. The store answers 404 for all three; the operator screen rendered the missing statements as `not read`.\\n\\nRetires: the doctor's `done` on an unattested traversal; `not read` as the rendering of a statement that does not exist.\\n\\n## Claims\\n\\n- bin/attavo\\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\\n- attavo.toml\\n- .attavo/bin/forge-attestation\\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml\\n- tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\\n- tests/test_doctor.py\\n- tests/test_record_schemas.py\\n\\n## Criteria\\n\\n- doctor-fails-on-an-unsealed-merge.sh: on a fixture tenant with two merged items whose [forge].attestation_command answers for one merge and not the other, attavo doctor --json fails proof every-attested-item-is-sealed naming item 2 and its merge sha, listing sealed and unsealed, and holds once the command answers for both\\n- doctor-fails-without-attestation-command.sh: a manifest with no [forge].attestation_command fails the proof naming the key, and the manifest schema declares the key\\n- the-proof-has-its-test.sh: a test named test_doctor_proof_six_fails_on_an_unsealed_merge exists under tests/, this repository's manifest names its attestation command, and .attavo/bin/forge-attestation is executable\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-wT2xhNpT' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-ectuhLhO' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n## Problem\\n\\n`attavo doctor` reported done on this repository on 2026-09-17 while none of its three traversals (#106, #148, #153) had a statement in the attestation store: `main` had classic protection and no merge que